From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bridger: invalidate member flows when bridge policy changes

Bridge VLAN filtering and protocol changes affect every member port.
Clear flows throughout the bridge FDB when updating the bridge device,
including flows between ports that are not attached to its own FDB list.

Do not insert an existing member into the same list again when its
master has not changed.

Signed-off-by: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
---
--- a/device.c
+++ b/device.c
@@ -246,6 +246,10 @@
 
 	list_for_each_entry(f, &dev->fdb_entries, dev_list)
 		fdb_clear_flows(f);
+
+	if (dev->br)
+		avl_for_each_element(&dev->br->fdb, f, node)
+			fdb_clear_flows(f);
 }
 
 void device_free(struct device *dev)
@@ -314,12 +318,10 @@
 			list_del_init(&dev->member_list);
 	}
 
-	if (master) {
-		if (master->br)
-			list_add_tail(&dev->member_list, &master->br->members);
-		else
-			master = NULL;
-	}
+	if (master && !master->br)
+		master = NULL;
+	if (master && dev->master != master)
+		list_add_tail(&dev->member_list, &master->br->members);
 
 	if (dev->master != master)
 		D("Set device %s master to %s\n", dev->ifname,
